## Summary

`ResultChart.tsx` builds the class name for chart text marks as `result-chart-${variant}`, special-casing only `value` → `vallabel`. The renderers emit category labels with `variant: 'cat'` (bar, hbar, line) and the axis unit with `variant: 'unit'`. The resulting classes are `result-chart-cat` and `result-chart-unit`, but `frontend/app/globals.css` styles `.result-chart-catlabel`, which no element receives, and has no rule for `.result-chart-unit`.

With no `fill` rule, the SVG text uses the default black fill. In light mode that happens to look acceptable. With `prefers-color-scheme: dark`, the category labels (for example, customer names on an hbar chart) are black on a near-black background and effectively invisible. Tick and value labels are unaffected because their class names match.

Seen on v1.2.0, and the same code is on `main` at c447003.

## Steps to reproduce

1. Set the OS or browser to dark mode. The app follows `prefers-color-scheme` and has no in-app theme toggle.
2. Ask any question that returns a categorical bar or hbar chart, for example *"Who were our top 5 customers by invoiced revenue in 2016?"*
3. The y-axis category labels are not readable. `getComputedStyle(document.querySelector('svg text.result-chart-cat')).fill` returns `rgb(0, 0, 0)`.

## Cause

```tsx
// frontend/components/ResultChart/ResultChart.tsx:229
className={`result-chart-${mark.variant === 'value' ? 'vallabel' : mark.variant}`}
```

```css
/* frontend/app/globals.css:321 */
.result-chart-tick,
.result-chart-vallabel,
.result-chart-catlabel {        /* never matches: the element class is result-chart-cat */
	fill: var(--result-chart-muted);
	font-size: 10px;
}
```

## Suggested fix

The smallest fix adds the selectors that are actually emitted:

```diff
 .result-chart-tick,
 .result-chart-vallabel,
-.result-chart-catlabel {
+.result-chart-catlabel,
+.result-chart-cat,
+.result-chart-unit {
 	fill: var(--result-chart-muted);
 	font-size: 10px;
 }
```

Alternatively, map `cat` → `catlabel` in `ResultChart.tsx` alongside `value` → `vallabel`, and give `unit` its own rule. With the CSS change, the labels compute to `rgb(161, 161, 170)` (`--result-chart-muted` in dark mode) and are readable in both themes.
